# PROJECT_SUMMARY.md synchronization

For any task where repository files are changed, update `PROJECT_SUMMARY.md` so it reflects the new state of the project before completing.

- Keep a top-level section describing the current project state and architecture.
- Add a concise list of changed/added/removed files.
- Record new dependencies, scripts, and configuration updates.
- Record outstanding work, risks, and known issues introduced by changes.
- If `PROJECT_SUMMARY.md` is missing, create it and include the above details.
- If the summary already exists, update it in place and note why each changed area now differs.
- If the change introduces multiple independent updates, include a short “Current status” section that mentions the combined effect.
